# Large binary and data artifacts go to Git LFS, so cloning the repository does
# not drag their full history along with it.
#
# Only genuinely large files belong here. Everything smaller stays in git
# proper: LFS costs bandwidth quota on every fetch, including every CI run, so
# adding a 300 KB file buys nothing and costs something.
#
# Currently tracked:
#   data/example.tsv           ~17 MB  the parallel corpus
#   data/pretrained/model.pt   ~10 MB  the checkpoint tutorial 5 loads
#
# CI deliberately checks out WITHOUT LFS, so these arrive as ~130-byte pointer
# files there. That is a supported state, not a broken one: the tests that read
# them skip, and the notebook gate skips the tutorials that need them. Anything
# reading a tracked artifact must tolerate a pointer rather than assume content.
# A developer with a normal clone gets the real files and runs the full set.
data/example.tsv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Notebooks are text and diff better without normalization surprises.
*.ipynb -text
